<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="MTG3" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Graphing #3</title>

    <objectives>
                    <ul>
                        <li>    <p>
                    <alert>G #3:</alert> I can describe a situation given a qualitative graph 
                    with defined inputs and outputs.     
                </p></li>
            </ul>
            
    </objectives>

    <exercise>
        <introduction>
        <p>
            The graph below shows the distance from the starting line for one runner in a race.  Use the information in 
            the graph to answer the questions that follow.
        </p>
        <image source="midtermgraph.png" width="40%">
            <shortdescription>A graph showing the position of a runner at given times.</shortdescription>
        </image>
        </introduction>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    At which of the marked points is the runner moving towards the finish line?  (Select all that apply)
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    The vertical axis shows the distance from the starting line, so the runner is moving toward the finish
                    line when the function is increasing, which happens at points A and E. 
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    At which of the marked points is the runner stopped? (Select all that apply)
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    The runner is stopped when on a horizontal line, which occurs at point C.
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
        <task workspace="0.25in">
            <statement>
                <p>
                    At which of the marked points is the runner moving the fastest?  (Select all that apply)
                </p>
            </statement>
            <solution>
                <p>
                    The runner is moving the fastest when the line is the steepest, which occurs at point E.
                </p>
            </solution>
        </task>
    </exercise>

</worksheet>